{"kind":"report","text":"# Private browser Join custody — correction 2\n\n2026-10-09. Read-only successor to report2e414bfb under original request\n934a632a0505874dbcd2bf8f6961fc4a2b1247c7 / promise\n808815b73d322e8b92af99e886d4a3c2b6b4f822. Addresses checker report\nf5f712fc38ae02a8b2d54bde7949bee166a315fa in full. The earlier contract's\nnative Join, exact binding/signing, all-entry-path custody, answer-first\nretention, original-key settlement and access/readiness separation remain.\nNo source edits, tests, runtime, gate, protocol adoption or broad C4 closure.\n\n## One shared metadata and capacity owner\n\nUse one authoritative canonical private localStorage journal value, not an\nindependently updated index plus per-record values. It holds version, generation,\nrecords keyed by actual enrollment identity, identity/operation lookup metadata,\nand fixed capacity reservations. Capacity accounting adds reserved64KiB per\nslot plus measured canonical top-level/index metadata, rather than counting\nonly each currently short payload. The lookup index is derived and validated\nfrom the records on every read; it never authorizes deletion, replacement,\nabsence or submission. Scope of this journal is exactly browser Join custody.\nNo generic outbox, claim journal or new storage backend is introduced.\n\nAll participants use mandatory Web Locks. Fixed order: acquire the enrollment\nlock first (normalized serving origin + full membership incarnation + keyID),\nthen acquire the ONE origin-wide Join metadata/budget lock. Never acquire any\nenrollment lock while holding that metadata lock, and never acquire two\nenrollment locks at once. Same-identity lock may span native network/recovery;\nthe global metadata lock covers only bounded read/validate/change/canonical\nwrite/readback and releases BEFORE every native/network await. A different\nidentity can make progress while the first waits for a network answer.\n\nUnder the global lock, read the complete journal within its raw character and\nUTF-8 allowance BEFORE parsing; strict shape/signature/binding checks precede\nuse. A new operation reserves one slot and its maximum record allowance before\nbuilding/signing; the unsigned binding/reservation is kept first. Building\nthen occurs under the enrollment lock and the completed exact envelope is\nwritten/read back under the global lock before dispatch. A crash after the\nunsigned reservation leaves a reserved-but-unprepared operation, not a\npermission to infer no earlier external history or recycle another record. Each slot reserves64KiB INCLUDING signed envelope,\nknown-answer history, observations and selection metadata. The shared journal\nis at most64records and4MiB raw UTF-8 INCLUDING index/generation/reservation\nmetadata. Capacity admission checks the canonical proposed whole journal's\nsize and reserved-growth ledger;64times64KiB plus metadata cannot fit4MiB,\nso effective admission may be fewer than64. Do not call64 a guaranteed count.\nA per-record or journal overflow refuses before signing/POST; preserve every\nunresolved record and raw bytes. No evictions or implicit replacement.\n\nEach record reserves growth before mutation: proposed64KiB splits into\n32KiB original binding/envelope/credential-reference,16KiB native answer,\n8KiB observation/selection and8KiB record/reservation metadata. Canonical\nUTF-8 serialization, including JSON escaping, must fit each allocation; a\nnew-envelope bound failure sends nothing and retains its unsigned reservation\nuntil explicit never-dispatched release under this owner. The same64KiB\nreservation stays charged through acceptance and unknown outcomes; extra observations replace their latest observation\nonly, never the original request or known native answer. Reject unsupported\nreply/metadata growth before dispatch when its declared maximum cannot fit.\nIf an actual answer exceeds the reserved supported shape/size, preserve the\noriginal attempted request and in-memory known answer, report local retention\nunavailable, and do not admit another operation to consume its reservation.\nNo truncation or dropped accepted fact earns a confirmed recovery claim.\n\nPersist the whole operation prepared record/reservation in ONE setItem and\nverify readback while holding the metadata lock. Then persist attempted:true\nin another whole-journal write/readback immediately before POST. Readers treat\neither saved state conservatively; attempted may have been sent and must\nreconcile. Atomic replacement of one value avoids split record/index writes.\nCrash after preparation consumes a slot; crash after attempted consumes the\nfull unknown reservation; crash after acceptance before answer write keeps\nattempted custody and settles the original request. On reload, recompute the\nledger/index from validated retained records. A mismatch, corrupt/oversized\njournal, or partial legacy migration makes the journal unavailable; retain its\noriginal bytes and refuse new work. No reconstruction from missing fragments.\nIf whole write succeeds but readback fails, local state is indeterminate and\nno POST begins; preserve the prior and candidate bytes in memory for explicit\nreconciliation. Cross-tab cooperating access is serialized; arbitrary\nsame-origin scripts/storage tampering are outside this lock guarantee.\n\n## Lost history is distinct from missing credential\n\nA retained valid operation plus missing original key is identifiable:\n“Original enrollment retained; original key unavailable. No new enrollment\nwas sent.” Fence that retained enrollment identity, preserve envelope/answer,\nand permit only native read paths the original custody still authorizes.\nCorrupt retained bytes mean “Local Join recovery record unavailable”; retain\nraw bytes and block new Join under the shared journal until repair. Do not\npretend its unvalidated identity or acceptance is proven.\n\nAn absent/cleared journal AND absent index/key/history cannot identify an\noriginal operation or prove first use. Say “Prior enrollment history is\nunknown; local recovery is unavailable.” Do not claim one specific operation\nis retained/fenced, do not say no prior POST occurred, and do not generate a\nnew key/signature or send Join merely because local storage is empty. A\npersisted first-use marker in the same storage is equally erasable and cannot\nsolve this. Current first-use invitation UI must represent this missing\nhistory condition until an explicit authorized recovery/start decision exists.\n\nExternal recovery requires independently retained original full binding,\nexact signed envelope or native fact/proof and ORIGINAL signing-key custody.\nVerify origin, directory/membership incarnation, actor/key, invitation and\nnative pin before original-key settlement or identical resubmission. External\nproof of acceptance does not manufacture the lost private key or current\naccess. No admin/operator key transfer, assumed same-member identity or\nfresh enrollment from an empty-store inference. The existing wider C4\nidentity/enrollment owner must define any authorized new-start/re-enrollment\ndecision; this narrow contract adopts no such service or recovery protocol.\n\n## Required two-identity and loss witnesses\n\n1. Two tabs with DIFFERENT membership/key identities race the final available\nslot/byte reservation. Both use their own enrollment lock, then the shared\nmetadata lock. One atomic reservation wins; the loser reads the new ledger,\nrefuses capacity before signing/POST, and leaves the winner's exact raw unknown\nrecord untouched. Repeat conceptually for answer growth while another identity\nreserves work: fixed maximum reservation prevents overcommit. This is one\nfocused fixture with a deterministic lock gate, no sleeps or field sweep.\n2. Crash gates before whole write, after prepared write, after attempted write\nand after native accepted reply show index/ledger recovery from the SAME\ncanonical journal; no shared index lost update and no second native envelope.\nGlobal lock is released during network wait, verified by the second identity's\nbounded reservation/refusal completing while the first answer is held.\n3. Distinguish valid record+missing key, corrupt record, and entirely absent\njournal/index/key. Only the first names a retained original enrollment; both\nlatter cases block new POST but use different truthful recovery language.\nRestore independently retained original envelope/key into the authorized\nrecovery path, settle exact original acceptance, and never infer a new member.\n\nALL Settings Join and invitationTask POST paths must delegate through this\nsame custody owner; no unjournaled wrapper remains. Browser origin-private\nextractable key and same-origin exposure remain as before. Actual revocation\nwindows, cross-device/non-extractable keys and hosted cold-browser acceptance\nkeep their existing C4/C5/C6 owners. Runtime commission follows exact review\nand adoption; this document supplies neither implementation nor acceptance.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:808815b73d322e8b92af99e886d4a3c2b6b4f822 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:00a6f83a0f12d69721bf0bd026b14608ffac8a31, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0148a0176116a4fb5401c96dbbb813a144b65616, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0357a3c97289e2782ff1264563897f39ecb2ce42, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03f7bc46d133f1cde1f7936baaaa690a99416b97 and 56 more"}}